{
	"_units": "volume_l = litres, mass_kg = kilograms, capacity_l = storage added when worn. Plate *_vox sizes are 1 cm voxels. Armor: rating = level on Ballistics.LEVELS; material = ceramic, steel, polyethylene or composite; durability divides the integrity each hit takes (ArmorRules.INTEGRITY_LOSS); plate fits = carrier tiers it fits. Carriers (aramid soft armor): soft_rating, soft_faces (front, back, side), soft_parts (chest, abdomen), spall_cover (neck, face, arms). Magazines name their round in data/rounds.json; muzzle_velocity_mps overrides the round's for that barrel. Medical: treats = wound kinds it fixes, treat_s = seconds to apply (self_mult on yourself), rushed_s / remove_s = a rushed tourniquet and taking one off. Kits (IFAK, trauma kit) hold contents (item id: count); an opened kit keeps what is left in its state. Ammo: magazines and loose rounds (stats.loose) of the same calibre go together; volume_l and mass_kg of loose rounds are per round (packed), a magazine's mass_kg is full and empty_mass_kg empty. Smoke grenades name their cloud colour in smoke_colour (SmokeCloud.COLOURS). MOLLE: a carrier's molle lists its attach points (id; type mag, pistol, knife, radio, medical or utility; at = torso-local surface point in metres; face front, back, left or right). An attachable item names the point types it fits in attach. A pouch holds what accepts lists (item ids, type:x, tag:x; anything when absent) up to max_units and/or capacity_l litres (items of up to max_item_l each). People (PeopleLayer): zip cuffs take cuff_s to put on; intel items (type intel) carry an intel kind and a proposed intel_value, and each piece found gets its own intel_id in its state.",
